      "message": "yes ... but we should not do it here.\n\nwe don\u0027t really know, who else is using the clock / what kind of clock it is (dedicated RC / PLL /  system RC48). The way how power management work, we might want to remove at this point the bit preventing the deep-sleep / clock turn down:\ne.g. enable_sleep(SLEEP_MASK_USB_DEVICE);  (and the matching disable_sleep at resume)\n[by the way, this USB driver is kind of broken right now, I\u0027m seeing 0 disable_sleep() ...]\nif we have more complex clock scheme, a clock_enable_module(MODULE_USB, 0) might be good\n(and it\u0027s mostly harmless right now since it is stubbed on F0)",
